      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Did you ever get this sorted out Kazari? I work on a Mac too and have not run into this issue. Was it an issue with your project settings/Library?",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-02-03T04:10:28.449Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Yes I get it VRChat is not currently being developed on Mac but I know people like my self that are using Mac to do all they're development work. Every time I launch unity I have to go in to player settings to OpenGLCore and disable Metal as many shaders lack any support for that engine. Today I randomly thought to look into it and I found that EnvConfig is setting the Build target for Mac to null and is erasing any changes I make the engine settings. After I went and modified that file and set it to \"{ BuildTarget.StandaloneOSX, new UnityEngine.Rendering.GraphicsDeviceType[] { UnityEngine.Rendering.GraphicsDeviceType.OpenGLCore } }\" now unity launches correctly without issue. It would be really cool if the SDK was updated to set the correct engine as its only a single line change and should not affect the game as it only effects Mac users. Thanks",
